; The Z rail look is the shared item look below; the rail only hides until its course view is open.
pub const CSS_ZR : str =".zr{display:none}";
; With no hash the first course is open (Y1 Courses, X1 the first course, Z1 its first lesson): its Z rail shows, and any marker
; hides it again; the course rules that follow (ids) show the Z rail of the course that is really open.
pub const CSS_ZR_DEFAULT : str = "#z-t27-basics{display:flex}.st:target~main #z-t27-basics{display:none}";
; Tab 1 of X and of Z is selected by default, the same white fill as the lit rule, and any other selection takes it back:
; X1 when another course is the marker, Z1 while another Z item holds the focus (a Z press moves the focus onto it).
pub const CSS_DEFAULT_SEL : str = ".x [href='#v-t27-basics'],.zr a:first-child";
pub const CSS_DEFAULT_OFF : str = ".st:target~main .x [href='#v-t27-basics']:not(:hover),.zr:focus-within a:first-child:not(:focus):not(:hover)";
; ONE object (owner 2026-11-21): Y, Z, the display and X sit in one frame, drawn once by .app::after over rows 2 to 4 of
; the grid: a single 1px line, one outer edge, no boxes and no gaps between the menus, only the 1px divider under Y,
; right of Z and over X. The header stays above the frame, the hero strip and the footer below it.
